ALCF patch 0002: record the torchcomms version/build tag in the CSV

Two bugs, one line apart.

1. Upstream computes

       try:
           torchcomms_version = torchcomms.__version__
       except AttributeError:
           torchcomms_version = "unknown"

   into a LOCAL variable and never assigns it to info.torchcomms_version.
   The dataclass default ("n/a") therefore survives into every CSV row.
   Confirmed in our Phase 2 output: TorchCommsVersion=n/a on all rows.

2. Even fixed, the lookup is empty on our build -- the installed torchcomms
   exposes no __version__ attribute at all. So a plain fix would just turn
   "n/a" into "unknown".

The patch assigns the field AND falls back to $TORCHCOMMS_BUILD_TAG, which
tc-perf-env populates from the frameworks module version. That makes CSVs
taken months apart, or across a frameworks upgrade, distinguishable -- which
is the entire point of having the column.

Not upstreamed: PR #2633 is a draft we assume will not merge.

--- a/collective_perf_test.py
+++ b/collective_perf_test.py
@@ -283,10 +283,17 @@
     else:
         info.device_name = "n/a"
 
-    try:
-        torchcomms_version = torchcomms.__version__
-    except AttributeError:
-        torchcomms_version = "unknown"
+    # ALCF patch 0002: actually record what was measured.
+    # Upstream computes a local `torchcomms_version` here and then never
+    # assigns it to info.torchcomms_version, so every CSV reports "n/a".
+    # Worse, some builds (ours included) ship no torchcomms.__version__ at
+    # all, so even the fixed lookup yields nothing useful -- hence the
+    # TORCHCOMMS_BUILD_TAG fallback, which tc-perf-env sets from the
+    # frameworks module version.
+    torchcomms_version = getattr(torchcomms, "__version__", None)
+    if not torchcomms_version:
+        torchcomms_version = os.environ.get("TORCHCOMMS_BUILD_TAG", "unknown")
+    info.torchcomms_version = torchcomms_version
 
     if config.run_all_comm_adapters:
         adapters = ["torchcomms", "c10d", "c10d_torchcomms"]
